        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Stain or paint comes down to two questions: what does the concrete look like now, and how much moisture comes through it? A sound, attractive, possibly damp slab is a stain job. A patchy, dry slab where you want a clean solid color is a paint job. A garage that sees a car every day probably wants epoxy rather than either.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever way you go, test first. A plastic-sheet moisture test, a water-drop test for old sealer and a small sample patch of your chosen product will tell you more in a day than any product label. Spend the effort there, and both finishes can look good for years.
          </p>
